body:
The "No data source available" fallback can show even when the chart is actually driven by bound/static data (e.g., `useDataScope()` returns an empty array) because the condition only checks `!dataSource && schema.objectName && finalData.length === 0`. Consider gating this message on the absence of any explicit data inputs (e.g., only when `boundData` and `schema.data` are both null/undefined), so it doesn't misreport missing `dataSource` when data is intentionally provided via `bind`/`schema.data`.
```suggestion
  if (
      !dataSource &&
      schema.objectName &&
      finalData.length === 0 &&
      boundData == null &&
      schema.data == null
  ) {
```
